{"t": 1793258527.74395, "kind": "assistant", "content": "**Final design: P=9, Q=7, RNE**\n\n* `verify_rtl`: 0 mismatches / 1000 vectors\n* `synthesize_area`: block 26184 + acc 11604 = **37788 total**\n* vs baseline P=24 RNE exact-Q (25724 + 22044 = 47768):\n  * **total saving 9980 transistors = 20.9%**\n  * **accumulator saving 22044 -> 11604 = 10440 transistors = 47.4%**\n* `evaluate_accuracy confirm=true` (32 segments): **delta -0.13%** (14.357 vs 14.375 exact), well within +1.0% budget. Backup P=9 Q=8 RNE confirmed +0.41%.\n\n**What learned:**\n* **Q drives area, not P alone.** P 24->8 exact-Q only 22044->15556 acc. Adding Q=8 drops P=10 acc to 12414, P=8 to 11538. Cheapest to shrink adder/shifter via Q then P.\n* **Mode dominates accuracy.** RZ is catastrophic from bias accumulation: P8/Q8 RZ +1992% vs same P/Q RNE +1.08%; P6/Q6 RZ +3.8M% vs RNE +18%. RNE is mandatory; RZ never viable even at large P.\n* **Screening noise matters.** 4-seg +/-1.5% made P8/Q8 (+1.08%) look borderline and P9/Q8 (-1.43%) look best. Confirm on 32 segs resolved true order: P9/Q7 -0.13%, P9/Q8 +0.41%, allowing choice of smaller P9/Q7.\n", "tool_calls": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 768, "prompt_tokens": 8079, "total_tokens": 8847, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 384}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 6257}}}
